<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mons Graupius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">83 or 84</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-conquest-of-britain">Roman conquest of Britain</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> Graupius was fought in 83 or 84 CE in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> between a Roman army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-julius-agricola">Gnaeus Julius Agricola</a> and the Caledonians, whose leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> names as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calgacus">Calgacus</a>. Tacitus records a decisive Roman victory, but the site of the battle is unknown. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> did not follow it with a lasting conquest of the far north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-graupius.jpg" alt="Battle of Mons Graupius" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: myself · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agricola.Campaigns.80.84.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
